{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-10{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+20x+36y=64?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}+20x+36y & =64 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+36y-10{x}^{2}+20x & =64 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}+4y]-10[{x}^{2}-2x] & =64 \\\\ 9[(y+2)^{2}-4]-10[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =64 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-36-10(x-1)^{2}+10 & =64 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-10(x-1)^{2} & =64+36-10 \\\\ 9(y+2)^{2}-10(x-1)^{2} & =90 \\\\ \\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(1,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08283654b18d4f3db96e73000f824a9f15e18318a753ff27764d0667804ac18d"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-1)"] ["math" "(-2,-2)"] ["math" "(-2,1)"] ["math" "(1,-2)"] ["math" "(2,-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-16380" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(1,-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n${x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}+6x+48y=71?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}+6x+48y & =71 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x-8{y}^{2}+48y & =71 \\\\ [{x}^{2}+6x]-8[{y}^{2}-6y] & =71 \\\\ [(x+3)^{2}-9]-8[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =71 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-9-8(y-3)^{2}+72 & =71 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}-8(y-3)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{8}-(y-3)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-3,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08283654b18d4f3db96e73000f824a9f15e18318a753ff27764d0667804ac18d"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,3)"] ["math" "(1,-8)"] ["math" "(3,-3)"] ["math" "(3,3)"] ["math" "(8,1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-116107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-3,3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=4$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,4,-3\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08283654b18d4f3db96e73000f824a9f15e18318a753ff27764d0667804ac18d"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328280" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y & =7 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-2y) & =7 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-1)^{2}+1 & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =7+4-1 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5/2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,1\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b800223a98b303b42b3e246d287a60ebb7"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08283654b18d4f3db96e73000f824a9f15e18318a753ff27764d0667804ac18d"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013817/state.json" "file_sha256" "87ee84d0a5501ad951f06e8bddc3d8b